            <div class="card"><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">⌂</span><h3>Sri Agastyar Peedam (Ashram)</h3></div><p>Sri Agastyar Peedam (Ashram) has been managed by 5 generations of initiated Nadi readers. Daily pujas for Sri Agastya Bhagawan and His consort, Sri Lopamudra Devi are done on all days of the year. The Peedam or Ashram is maintained with the sanctity of a temple.</p><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">☷</span><h3>Our Services</h3></div><div class="service-grid"><div class="service-box"><h4>Nadi Reading</h4><p>Authentic Nadi readings revealing your past, present and future based on ancient manuscripts preserved for centuries.</p></div><div class="service-box"><h4>Prasnam</h4><p>Prasnam means Question. Through Prasnam, answers and remedies for a specific question are obtained through an intricate traditional ritual.</p></div></div></div>
            <div class="story-grid"><div class="portrait"><img data-speak role="button" tabindex="0" src="{{ asset('images/author.jpeg') }}" alt="Agastya and Lopamudra Devi"><div class="portrait-caption"><h3>GURUJI SIVA MARIMUTHU - CHIEF NADI ASTROLOGY</h3><p>One of the few original Nadi Readers in India</p></div></div><div class="story"><h3>Our Story</h3><p>GURUJI SIVA MARIMUTHU - CHIEF NADI ASTROLOGY is a 5th generation Nadi Reader. He has been initiated into Siva and Agastya deekshas and performs austerities daily, as instructed by his deeksha guru.</p><p>He is completely dedicated to reading Nadi leaves strictly according to ancient customs and will not compromise on the processes involved in Nadi reading, regardless of monetary gains or losses.</p></div></div>
            <div class="card nadi-note"><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">▤</span><h3>Nadi Reading vs Astrology</h3></div><p>Nadi Reading is NOT to be confused with astrology.</p><p>Nadi Reading is reading of ancient manuscripts or Nadi leaves that are associated with you. It is based on the vision of ancient sages like Sri Agastya Bhagawan as well as instructions of Lord Shiva. It is NOT dependent on any planetary positions. Nadi readings relate to your soul's past journeys, current journey or lifetime and future lifetime.</p><p>It looks at your prarabdha karma, or the karmas you were born with. Remedies or pariharams suggested in your Nadi leaves aim to lessen the impact of those karmas and address issues that could arise in the future. Nadi remedies deal not only with the nine navagrahas, but also with various deities.</p><p>Astrology is based on individual horoscopes drawn from the time and place of birth and the planetary positions at the time of birth. Horoscope-related charts and readings are based entirely on planetary positions and mostly involve remedies related to the nine navagrahas.</p></div>
            <div class="card process"><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">☷</span><h3>Nadi Reading Process</h3></div><ol><li>Call, email, or send a WhatsApp message asking for help with Nadi reading for yourself or your family.</li><li>The administrator or Nadi Reader GURUJI SIVA MARIMUTHU - CHIEF NADI ASTROLOGY will give instructions on which thumbprints should be sent by email or WhatsApp.</li><li>Based on the thumbprints, a subset of Nadi manuscripts will be selected.</li><li>A prasnam will be done to ask Sri Agastya Bhagawan for permission to look at your leaves.</li><li>If permission is not given, you will be informed and may be advised to approach again after a year or two.</li><li>If permission is received, the Nadi Reader will give you an appointment for a call or in-person visit.</li><li>During the meeting, you will be asked questions to finalize the primary set of leaves associated with you.</li><li>If your leaves cannot be finalized after an extensive search, you may be asked to contact the Peedam again in six months.</li><li>If your leaves are finalized, you will be asked to make one payment for the reading of your past, current, and future life.</li><li>Payment can be made in cash, GPay, or bank transfer. The Peedam does not accept credit or debit cards and payments are made in Indian Rupees.</li><li>Once payment is received, the Nadi Reader will arrange an appointment for the high-level reading and identify a secondary set of leaves.</li><li>Once the secondary leaves are identified, another appointment may be arranged for the detailed reading.</li><li>The detailed reading explains the years of your life, challenges, good fortunes, and relevant guidance.</li><li>Pariharams or remedies may be suggested, including temple visits, pilgrimage, feeding cows, or helping people in need.</li><li>Guidance needed to complete the pariharams will be provided by the Nadi Reader or Peedam administrator.</li></ol></div>
            <div class="two-col" style="margin-top:4rem"><div class="card"><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">◎</span><h3>Languages We Understand</h3></div><p>Primarily, readings are conducted in Tamil. Through translators at Sri Agastyar Peedam, we can assist clients in:</p><ul class="content-list"><li>English</li><li>Malayalam</li><li>Telugu</li><li>Kannada</li><li>Hindi</li></ul><p>Over the years, we have worked with and continue to serve clients from around 66 countries.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="card-heading"><span class="icon">◷</span><h3>Hours of Operation</h3></div><p>We are open to help clients from Monday through Friday from 9 am to 7 pm and on Saturdays by appointment.</p><p>Agastyar Peedam is closed for clients during all Hindu festivals and New Year's day, although daily pujas continue on all days of the year.</p></div></div>
